				11,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mist): Clarify TODOs as DEPENDENCY comments for Hickory DNS\n\nThis commit updates comment prefixes in server.rs and zone.rs from `TODO:` to `DEPENDENCY:` to more accurately reflect the nature of the outstanding work.\n\nThe NxProofKind configuration for DNSSEC NSEC/NSEC3 support and the record insertion implementation via the Authority trait's update method are dependent on the upstream Hickory DNS library's API and behavior, rather than being internal implementation tasks.\n\nThis clarification helps distinguish between internal implementation work (TODOs) and external library dependencies (DEPENDENCIES) that may require upstream contributions or version updates to resolve.",
			"SHA": "50f8db403fb6d0cafd5d439ccd48697c97da6df4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-27T10:04:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⣿⡏⠀",
				11,
				8
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mist): Introduce DNS isolation element for private network\n\nThis commit introduces **Mist**, a new DNS server element for the Land Code Editor that provides secure DNS isolation and private network resolution.\n\n## Overview\n\nMist is a complete DNS server implementation built on the Hickory DNS library that creates a secure sandbox for resolving `*.editor.land` domains exclusively to localhost (127.0.0.1). This ensures all private network communication remains local and cannot leak to external networks.\n\n## Architecture Integration\n\nThis new element integrates with the Land ecosystem as follows:\n\n- **Mountain**: Will start the DNS server during application initialization and provide the port to other components via the `DnsPort` managed state.\n- **Air**: Uses the DNS server for secure HTTP requests, configuring HTTP clients to use the local DNS resolver.\n- **SideCar**: Spawns Node.js sidecars with DNS override configuration, ensuring all DNS queries go through the local server.\n- **Cocoon**: The Node.js extension host can resolve `editor.land` domains via the local DNS server for gRPC communication with Mountain.\n\n## Key Components\n\n- **`server.rs`**: Core DNS server implementation using Hickory, handles UDP/TCP listeners bound exclusively to loopback (127.0.0.1) with comprehensive security validation.\n- **`zone.rs`**: Authoritative zone configuration for `editor.land` with SOA, NS, and A records all pointing to loopback addresses.\n- **`resolver.rs`**: Provides `LandDnsResolver` implementing `reqwest::dns::Resolve` for HTTP client integration with defense-in-depth IP validation.\n- **`forward_security.rs`**: Forward allowlist restricting external DNS queries to trusted domains (update.editor.land, cdn.crashlytics.com).\n- **`lib.rs`**: Public API entry point with `start()` and `dns_port()` functions.\n\n## Security Features\n\n1. **Loopback-only binding**: Server binds exclusively to 127.0.0.1, preventing LAN access\n2. **Defense-in-depth IP validation**: Resolver enforces 127.x.x.x for editor.land domains\n3. **Forward allowlist**: Only permits external resolution to explicitly trusted domains\n4. **DNSSEC-ready**: Zone signing infrastructure (ECDSA P-256) is configured\n\nThis establishes the foundation for secure local service discovery and gRPC communication within the Land ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "6db973f388107c7e8477d1c6c11c5ab923ed164b"
		}
	],
